{% doc %}
  @prompt
    Create a premium, fully responsive and highly customizable editorial lifestyle section for the luxury wellness brand "Elqorin".
    
    IMPORTANT:
    - This section is for ELQORIN, NOT Soluna.
    - Do not modify or depend on the hero section.
    - Do not make the entire section an image background.
    - Only the three lifestyle cards should contain images.
    - Build this as a reusable Shopify theme section with proper Theme Editor settings.
    - Do not hard-code the layout or content.
    
    DESIGN REFERENCE / STRUCTURE:
    
    The section should closely follow this structure:
    
    DESKTOP:
    - Warm off-white / cream section background.
    - Two-column editorial layout.
    - Left column approximately 27% width.
    - Right column approximately 73% width.
    - Left column contains:
      - Small uppercase eyebrow
      - Large editorial heading
      - Supporting paragraph
    - Right column contains 3 equal image cards in one horizontal row.
    - Cards have small gaps between them.
    - Cards use full-bleed lifestyle imagery.
    - Images should have a subtle dark gradient/overlay for readability.
    - Category label positioned near the top-left.
    - Supporting copy positioned near the bottom-left.
    - Clean luxury editorial aesthetic.
    - Minimal borders.
    - Very subtle or no shadows.
    - Sharp or subtly rounded card corners.
    - Generous whitespace.
    - Typography should feel premium, modern and understated.
    
    DEFAULT CONTENT:
    
    Section eyebrow:
    THE PROBLEM
    
    Heading:
    Your body keeps the score.
    Your schedule doesn't make room for it.
    
    Description:
    Work. Training. Family. Life doesn't slow down. Recovery shouldn't have to wait for the weekend.
    
    CARD 1:
    Label:
    WORK
    
    Text:
    Long hours.
    High demands.
    
    CARD 2:
    Label:
    TRAINING
    
    Text:
    You push hard.
    Your body pays.
    
    CARD 3:
    Label:
    LIFE
    
    Text:
    Responsibilities
    never stop.
    
    The content above should only be the default content. Everything must remain editable.
    
    IMAGE DIRECTION:
    
    Use premium, realistic lifestyle photography appropriate for a high-ticket wellness/recovery brand.
    
    CARD 1 — WORK:
    A sophisticated professional working long hours at home or in a premium office environment. The person should look mentally tired or physically drained, but the image should remain aspirational and premium.
    
    CARD 2 — TRAINING:
    An athletic person after an intense workout, sitting/resting in a premium training environment. Show physical fatigue and recovery need without looking like a fitness advertisement.
    
    CARD 3 — LIFE:
    A sophisticated parent or professional with family responsibilities. The image should communicate that life continues even when the body needs recovery.
    
    Avoid generic stock-photo aesthetics.
    Avoid cheesy smiling wellness imagery.
    Use cinematic lighting, realistic environments, premium photography and restrained composition.
    
    FULL CUSTOMIZATION IS MANDATORY:
    
    Every meaningful visual/content aspect must be configurable from Shopify Theme Editor without editing code.
    
    SECTION SETTINGS:
    - Background color
    - Text color
    - Section top padding
    - Section bottom padding
    - Desktop padding
    - Mobile padding
    - Desktop content/card gap
    - Mobile content/card gap
    - Desktop text column width
    - Card gap
    - Card border radius
    - Card image height
    - Image overlay opacity
    - Desktop text alignment
    - Mobile text alignment
    
    TEXT SETTINGS:
    - Eyebrow text
    - Heading
    - Heading size
    - Heading tag (H1-H6)
    - Description
    - Text alignment
    - Maximum text width
    
    CARD BLOCK SETTINGS:
    
    Do NOT hard-code exactly three cards.
    
    Create repeatable Shopify blocks so merchants can:
    - Add cards
    - Remove cards
    - Duplicate cards
    - Reorder cards
    
    Each card must independently support:
    - Desktop image
    - Mobile image
    - Image focal position
    - Label/category
    - Card text
    - Text alignment
    - Overlay opacity
    - Optional link
    - Optional button label
    - Button URL
    - Button style
    - Card background fallback color
    - Card border radius if supported
    
    Make all card settings independent. Changing one card must not affect the others.
    
    RESPONSIVE DESIGN IS MANDATORY:
    
    Desktop:
    - Two-column layout.
    - Approximately 27% text / 73% cards.
    - Cards displayed horizontally.
    
    Tablet:
    - Reduce spacing and typography proportionally.
    - Keep cards readable and visually balanced.
    - Never allow cards to overlap or become clipped.
    
    Mobile:
    - Switch to a single-column layout.
    - Text content appears first.
    - Cards appear below the text.
    - Default mobile behavior should stack cards vertically.
    - If implementing horizontal scrolling as an option, make it configurable through the Theme Editor.
    - Cards must remain large enough for the imagery and text to be visually effective.
    - Use separate mobile image settings where available.
    - Use separate mobile typography and spacing settings.
    
    TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS:
    
    - Use semantic HTML.
    - Use CSS Grid/Flexbox for layout.
    - Do not use absolute positioning for the primary layout.
    - Do not use fixed pixel coordinates to position text or cards.
    - Do not create a desktop-only design and simply shrink it on mobile.
    - Use responsive CSS and clamp() where appropriate.
    - Use Shopify's native section/block schema corre, Modify the CURRENT section you just created. Do not create a new section.
    
    The current structure is correct, but the visual execution needs to be substantially improved to match the provided reference.
    
    IMPORTANT: This is ELQORIN, a premium high-ticket wellness/recovery brand. Do NOT reference or use Soluna branding.
    
    VISUAL CORRECTIONS:
    
    1. CARD IMAGES
    The three cards must use real image_picker settings and display the selected images as full-bleed photography.
    
    Do NOT use gradients, grey placeholders, illustrations, generated patterns, or the existing placeholder artwork as the primary card image.
    
    Each card must have:
    - Desktop image picker
    - Optional mobile image picker
    - object-fit: cover
    - image-position control
    - subtle dark gradient overlay only for text readability
    
    If no image is selected, show a clean neutral placeholder, but never generate a fake grey gradient as the card image.
    
    2. CARD PROPORTIONS
    
    Change the cards from tall/narrow portrait cards to wider editorial landscape cards.
    
    Desktop:
    - Three cards in one row
    - Equal width
    - Approximately 2:1 to 1.5:1 visual ratio depending on available space
    - Cards should feel like premium editorial photography rather than tall product tiles
    - Maintain equal heights
    
    The cards should visually resemble the reference:
    wide rectangular lifestyle photography with text layered over the bottom portion.
    
    3. LEFT COLUMN
    
    Reduce the heading size substantially.
    
    The heading should read:
    
    Your body keeps the score.
    Your schedule doesn't make room for it.
    
    Use a refined editorial font size around 48–64px on desktop rather than the extremely large current heading.
    
    Use:
    font-weight: 400–500
    line-height: approximately 1.05–1.15
    
    Do not make the heading excessively bold.
    
    The left column should have enough width for natural line breaks.
    
    Target desktop structure:
    
    THE PROBLEM
    
    Your body keeps
    the score.
    Your schedule
    doesn't make
    room for it.
    
    Do not force every individual word onto separate lines.
    
    4. DESCRIPTION
    
    Keep:
    
    Work. Training. Family. Life doesn't slow down.
    Recovery shouldn't have to wait for the weekend.
    
    Use a smaller editorial body size around 16–18px with comfortable line height.
    
    5. CARD CONTENT
    
    Card 1:
    WORK
    
    Long hours.
    High demands.
    
    Card 2:
    TRAINING
    
    You push hard.
    Your body pays.
    
    Card 3:
    LIFE
    
    Responsibilities
    never stop.
    
    Position the label near the top-left.
    
    Position the supporting text near the bottom-left.
    
    Keep both inside the card with consistent padding.
    
    6. IMAGE OVERLAY
    
    The current grey/white gradient is far too strong.
    
    Use:
    - transparent upper area
    - subtle black gradient toward the bottom
    - approximately 20–45% maximum opacity at the bottom
    - no grey overlay
    - photography must remain clearly visible
    
    The card image should remain the dominant visual element.
    
    7. SECTION SPACING
    
    Use a premium editorial amount of whitespace.
    
    Desktop:
    - approximately 80–120px top/bottom padding
    - approximately 60–80px gap between text column and cards
    
    Do not make the section unnecessarily tall.
    
    8. RESPONSIVE DESIGN
    
    Desktop:
    - 27–30% text column
    - 70–73% cards
    - three cards in one row
    
    Tablet:
    - reduce typography and spacing
    - cards remain readable
    
    Mobile:
    - stack the text above the cards
    - cards become full-width
    - use approximately 4:3 or 3:2 card proportions
    - maintain readable card text
    - no overlapping
    - no horizontal page overflow
    
    Use CSS Grid/Flexbox.
    Do not use absolute positioning for the overall layout.
    
    9. FULL THEME EDITOR CUSTOMIZATION
    
    Keep all existing customization functionality.
    
    The merchant must be able to configure:
    
    SECTION:
    - background color
    - text color
    - desktop/mobile padding
    - text column width
    - column gap
    
    TEXT:
    - eyebrow
    - heading
    - description
    - heading size
    - heading weight
    - text alignment
    - maximum text width
    
    EACH CARD:
    - desktop image
    - mobile image
    - image position
    - label
    - text
    - text alignment
    - overlay opacity
    - optional link
    - optional button
    - button label
    - button URL
    - card radius
    
    CARD LAYOUT:
    - card gap
    - card height/aspect ratio
    - card radius
    
    Allow cards to be added, removed, duplicated and reordered.
    
    10. DO NOT BREAK THE THEME
    
    Scope all CSS to this section only.
    
    Do not modify:
    - header
    - hero
    - navigation
    - other sections
    - global typography
    - global buttons
    - global spacing
    
    The final result should look like a premium editorial section from a luxury wellness brand, not a generic Shopify card grid.
    
    MOST IMPORTANT:
    Use the selected Shopify images as actual background/full-bleed card imagery. The cards must look like real photography cards, not grey placeholders., Fix the existing section only. Do not create a new design and do not change the overall visual concept.
    
    The current section is supposed to match a premium luxury editorial layout:
    
    Desktop layout
    
    Full-width section with a warm off-white background.
    Maximum content width around 1280–1400px, centered.
    Two-column layout:
    Left column: approximately 30–32% width.
    Right column: approximately 68–70% width.
    Left column contains:
    Small uppercase eyebrow: THE PROBLEM
    Large editorial heading:
    Your body keeps the score. Your schedule doesn’t make room for it.
    Supporting paragraph:
    Work. Training. Family. Life doesn't slow down. Recovery shouldn't have to wait for the weekend.
    Right column contains exactly 3 equal cards in one horizontal row.
    Cards should be approximately 1:1.15–1:1.25 aspect ratio, not extremely tall.
    Cards should have rounded corners around 3–6px.
    Each card uses a real uploaded image as a full-card background image.
    Image must fill the entire card using object-fit: cover.
    Add a subtle dark gradient from transparent at the top to darker at the bottom so white text remains readable.
    Card content sits over the image:
    Eyebrow at the top-left: WORK, TRAINING, LIFE
    Bottom-left text:
    Long hours. High demands.
    You push hard. Your body pays.
    Responsibilities never stop.
    Do NOT use placeholder gradients, grey backgrounds, illustrations, or generated placeholder artwork.
    Do NOT put the image in a separate area inside the card. The image itself must be the card background.
    
    Critical sizing requirement
    
    Do NOT allow the left heading to become excessively narrow or wrap every few words.
    The heading should have a comfortable readable width and use a refined editorial font size around 48–64px on desktop.
    The three cards must remain visually dominant but should not become extremely tall.
    The entire section should feel similar in proportion to a high-end luxury ecommerce homepage, not an oversized dashboard component.
    
    Tablet
    
    Keep the two-column structure when space allows.
    Reduce heading size and gaps proportionally.
    Cards remain equal width.
    
    Mobile
    
    Stack the content vertically.
    Eyebrow + heading + paragraph first.
    Then the 3 cards vertically.
    Cards should have a reasonable mobile aspect ratio around 4:5 or 3:4.
    Never allow horizontal overflow.
    Do not squeeze the three cards into tiny columns.
    
    Theme editor requirements
    Make the entire section fully customizable through Shopify's theme editor.
    
    Section settings:
    
    Background color
    Content max width
    Section top/bottom padding
    Desktop column ratio
    Desktop heading size
    Mobile heading size
    Card gap
    Card border radius
    Card overlay opacity
    Card height/aspect ratio
    
    Text settings:
    
    Eyebrow
    Heading
    Description
    
    Each card must be an editable block with:
    
    Image picker
    Eyebrow text
    Main text
    Optional link
    Overlay opacity
    Text alignment
    
    Important implementation rules
    
    Preserve Shopify Online Store 2.0 compatibility.
    Use the theme's existing typography variables where possible.
    Use Liquid section blocks/settings rather than hardcoded content.
    Do not modify unrelated sections.
    Do not modify the header, hero, navigation, footer, or global styles.
    Scope all CSS to this section so it cannot affect other sections.
    Use responsive CSS with proper breakpoints.
    Do not use JavaScript unless absolutely necessary.
    Do not add animations that change the layout.
    Do not replace uploaded images with placeholders.
    
    Most important: The previous version incorrectly rendered the cards as tall grey gradient panels with the artwork floating inside them. That is wrong. Each card must display its assigned image edge-to-edge as the card background, with the text overlaid on top.
    
    Before finishing, verify:
    
    Desktop shows exactly 3 image cards beside the text.
    Images fill the cards completely.
    No grey placeholder gradients are visible when an image is assigned.
    Heading does not wrap into an excessively narrow column.
    Mobile stacks cleanly without overflow.
    Every setting is editable from the Shopify theme editor., change max height to 500px and make sure content is responsive enough to fit in it
{% enddoc %}
{% assign ai_gen_id = block.id | replace: '_', '' | downcase %}

{% style %}
  .ai-editorial-lifestyle-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: block;
    background-color: {{ block.settings.section_background }};
    color: {{ block.settings.section_text_color }};
    padding-top: {{ block.settings.section_padding_top_mobile }}px;
    padding-bottom: {{ block.settings.section_padding_bottom_mobile }}px;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .ai-editorial-lifestyle-container-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    max-width: {{ block.settings.max_width }}px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding-left: {{ block.settings.horizontal_padding_mobile }}px;
    padding-right: {{ block.settings.horizontal_padding_mobile }}px;
  }

  .ai-editorial-lifestyle-grid-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: {{ block.settings.content_gap_mobile }}px;
  }

  .ai-editorial-lifestyle-text-column-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: {{ block.settings.text_content_gap }}px;
    text-align: {{ block.settings.text_alignment_mobile }};
  }

  .ai-editorial-lifestyle-eyebrow-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: {{ block.settings.eyebrow_size_mobile }}px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: {{ block.settings.eyebrow_letter_spacing }}em;
    font-weight: {{ block.settings.eyebrow_weight }};
    color: {{ block.settings.eyebrow_color }};
    margin: 0;
  }

  .ai-editorial-lifestyle-heading-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: {{ block.settings.heading_size_mobile }}px;
    line-height: {{ block.settings.heading_line_height }};
    font-weight: {{ block.settings.heading_weight }};
    color: {{ block.settings.heading_color }};
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 100%;
    white-space: pre-line;
    {% if block.settings.text_alignment_mobile == 'center' %}
      margin-left: auto;
      margin-right: auto;
    {% endif %}
  }

  .ai-editorial-lifestyle-description-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: {{ block.settings.description_size_mobile }}px;
    line-height: {{ block.settings.description_line_height }};
    color: {{ block.settings.description_color }};
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 100%;
    {% if block.settings.text_alignment_mobile == 'center' %}
      margin-left: auto;
      margin-right: auto;
    {% endif %}
  }

  .ai-editorial-lifestyle-cards-column-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: {{ block.settings.card_gap_mobile }}px;
  }

  .ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: {{ block.settings.card_border_radius }}px;
    background-color: {{ block.settings.card_fallback_background }};
    height: {{ block.settings.card_min_height_mobile }}px;
    max-height: {{ block.settings.card_min_height_mobile }}px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease;
  }

  .ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-{{ ai_gen_id }}:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  .ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-image-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-overlay-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0) 0%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0) 50%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7) 100%);
    opacity: {{ block.settings.overlay_opacity | divided_by: 100.0 }};
    z-index: 2;
  }

  .ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-content-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 3;
    padding: {{ block.settings.card_padding }}px;
    color: {{ block.settings.card_text_color }};
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    height: 100%;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-label-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: {{ block.settings.card_label_size_mobile }}px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: {{ block.settings.card_label_letter_spacing }}em;
    font-weight: {{ block.settings.card_label_weight }};
    margin: 0;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-text-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    font-size: {{ block.settings.card_text_size_mobile }}px;
    line-height: {{ block.settings.card_text_line_height }};
    font-weight: {{ block.settings.card_text_weight }};
    margin: 0;
    white-space: pre-line;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-placeholder-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    z-index: 1;
    background-color: #e5e5e5;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-placeholder-{{ ai_gen_id }} svg {
    width: 50%;
    height: 50%;
    opacity: 0.15;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .ai-editorial-lifestyle-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      padding-top: {{ block.settings.section_padding_top_desktop }}px;
      padding-bottom: {{ block.settings.section_padding_bottom_desktop }}px;
    }

    .ai-editorial-lifestyle-container-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      padding-left: {{ block.settings.horizontal_padding_desktop }}px;
      padding-right: {{ block.settings.horizontal_padding_desktop }}px;
    }

    .ai-editorial-lifestyle-grid-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      grid-template-columns: {{ block.settings.text_column_width }}% 1fr;
      gap: {{ block.settings.content_gap_desktop }}px;
    }

    .ai-editorial-lifestyle-text-column-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      text-align: {{ block.settings.text_alignment_desktop }};
    }

    .ai-editorial-lifestyle-eyebrow-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      font-size: {{ block.settings.eyebrow_size_desktop }}px;
    }

    .ai-editorial-lifestyle-heading-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      font-size: {{ block.settings.heading_size_desktop }}px;
      max-width: {{ block.settings.heading_max_width }}px;
      {% if block.settings.text_alignment_desktop == 'center' %}
        margin-left: auto;
        margin-right: auto;
      {% elsif block.settings.text_alignment_desktop == 'left' %}
        margin-left: 0;
        margin-right: 0;
      {% else %}
        margin-left: auto;
        margin-right: 0;
      {% endif %}
    }

    .ai-editorial-lifestyle-description-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      font-size: {{ block.settings.description_size_desktop }}px;
      max-width: {{ block.settings.description_max_width }}px;
      {% if block.settings.text_alignment_desktop == 'center' %}
        margin-left: auto;
        margin-right: auto;
      {% elsif block.settings.text_alignment_desktop == 'left' %}
        margin-left: 0;
        margin-right: 0;
      {% else %}
        margin-left: auto;
        margin-right: 0;
      {% endif %}
    }

    .ai-editorial-lifestyle-cards-column-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      grid-template-columns: repeat({{ block.settings.cards_per_row_desktop }}, 1fr);
      gap: {{ block.settings.card_gap_desktop }}px;
    }

    .ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      height: {{ block.settings.card_min_height_desktop }}px;
      max-height: {{ block.settings.card_min_height_desktop }}px;
    }

    .ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-label-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      font-size: {{ block.settings.card_label_size_desktop }}px;
    }

    .ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-text-{{ ai_gen_id }} {
      font-size: {{ block.settings.card_text_size_desktop }}px;
    }
  }
{% endstyle %}

<editorial-lifestyle-{{ ai_gen_id }} class="ai-editorial-lifestyle-{{ ai_gen_id }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
  <div class="ai-editorial-lifestyle-container-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
    <div class="ai-editorial-lifestyle-grid-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
      <div class="ai-editorial-lifestyle-text-column-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
        {% if block.settings.eyebrow != blank %}
          <p class="ai-editorial-lifestyle-eyebrow-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
            {{ block.settings.eyebrow }}
          </p>
        {% endif %}

        {% if block.settings.heading != blank %}
          <{{ block.settings.heading_tag }} class="ai-editorial-lifestyle-heading-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
            {{ block.settings.heading }}
          </{{ block.settings.heading_tag }}>
        {% endif %}

        {% if block.settings.description != blank %}
          <div class="ai-editorial-lifestyle-description-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
            {{ block.settings.description }}
          </div>
        {% endif %}
      </div>

      <div class="ai-editorial-lifestyle-cards-column-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
        {% liquid
          assign card_1_link = block.settings.card_1_link
          assign card_2_link = block.settings.card_2_link
          assign card_3_link = block.settings.card_3_link
        %}

        {% if card_1_link != blank %}
          <a href="{{ card_1_link }}" class="ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
        {% else %}
          <div class="ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
        {% endif %}
          {% if block.settings.card_1_desktop_image != blank %}
            <picture>
              {% if block.settings.card_1_mobile_image != blank %}
                <source
                  media="(max-width: 749px)"
                  srcset="{{ block.settings.card_1_mobile_image | image_url: width: 800 }}"
                >
              {% endif %}
              <img
                src="{{ block.settings.card_1_desktop_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}"
                alt="{{ block.settings.card_1_desktop_image.alt | escape }}"
                loading="lazy"
                class="ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-image-{{ ai_gen_id }}"
                style="object-position: {{ block.settings.card_1_focal_point }};"
              >
            </picture>
          {% else %}
            <div class="ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-placeholder-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
              {{ 'lifestyle-1' | placeholder_svg_tag }}
            </div>
          {% endif %}
          <div class="ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-overlay-{{ ai_gen_id }}"></div>
          <div class="ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-content-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
            {% if block.settings.card_1_label != blank %}
              <p class="ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-label-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
                {{ block.settings.card_1_label }}
              </p>
            {% else %}
              <div></div>
            {% endif %}
            {% if block.settings.card_1_text != blank %}
              <p class="ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-text-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
                {{ block.settings.card_1_text }}
              </p>
            {% endif %}
          </div>
        {% if card_1_link != blank %}
          </a>
        {% else %}
          </div>
        {% endif %}

        {% if card_2_link != blank %}
          <a href="{{ card_2_link }}" class="ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
        {% else %}
          <div class="ai-editorial-lifestyle-card-{{ ai_gen_id }}">
        {% endif %}
          {% if block.settings.card_2_desktop_image != blank %}
            <picture>
              {% if block.settings.card_2_mobile_image != blank %}
                <source
                  media="(max-width: 749px)"
                  srcset="{{ block.settings.card_2_mobile_image | image_url: width: 800 }}"
                >
              {% endif %}
              <img
